{title: Stand Up, Stand Up for Jesus}
{artist: George Duffield Jr. / George J. Webb}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 113}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 99)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Stand up, stand up for [D]Jesus,
[D]Ye [A]soldiers [E]of [A]the [E]cross;
[E]Lift [A]high His royal [D]banner,
[D]It [A]must not [E7]suffer [A]loss.
[A]From [E]victory [F#m]un[E]to [A]victory
[A]His [D]army shall [Bm]He [A]lead,__[E]__
[E]Till [A]every foe is [D]vanquished,
[D]And [A]Christ is [E7]Lord in[A]deed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Stand up, stand up for [D]Jesus,
[D]The [A]solemn [E]watch[A]word [E]hear;
[E]If [A]while ye sleep He [D]suffers,
[D]A[A]way with [E7]shame and [A]fear;
[A]Wher[E]e’er ye [F#m]meet [E]with [A]evil,
[A]With[D]in you or [Bm]with[A]out,__[E]__
